<title>USA: TENNIS-RESULTS IN PHILADELPHIA MEN'S TOURNAMENT.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-RESULTS IN PHILADELPHIA MEN'S TOURNAMENT.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the $714,250</p>
<p>Advanta Championships men's tennis tournament on Monday</p>
<p>(prefix number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>First round:</p>
<p>3-Paul Haarhuis (Netherlands) beat Jiri Novak (Czech</p>
<p>Republic) 6-4 1-6 6-3</p>
<p>Sjeng Schalken (Netherlands) beat 5-Jason Stoltenberg</p>
<p>(Australia) 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>Juan Albert Viloca (Spain) beat 7-Alex O'Brien (U.S.) 6-2 3-6</p>
<p>6-3</p>
<p>Thomas Johansson (Sweden) beat 8-Greg Rusedski (Canada) 6-4</p>
<p>6-2</p>
<p>Kenneth Carlsen (Denmark) beat Tomas Carbonell (Spain) 4-6</p>
<p>6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Doug Flach (U.S.) beat Sebastien Lareau (Canada) 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>Justin Gimelstob (U.S.) beat Michael Joyce (U.S.) 6-0 6-3</p>
</text>
